-- title:
--   Base change of a finite Artin local ring along a flat ℤ-algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $C$ be a commutative ring which is local and Artinian and whose residue field $C/\mathfrak{m}_C$ is finite, and let $O$ be a commutative Noetherian ring which is flat as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module. Form the tensor product $C' := C \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} O$, regarded as a $C$-algebra and, via the inclusion $o \mapsto 1 \otimes o$, as an $O$-algebra. The theorem asserts the conjunction of four statements: (a) $C'$ is flat as a $C$-module; (b) the ring homomorphism underlying the $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra map `Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight` $: O \to C'$ is finite, i.e. $C'$ is generated as an $O$-module by finitely many elements; (c) $C'$ is a Noetherian ring; and (d) the ideal of $C'$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_C$ under the structure map $C \to C'$, namely $\mathfrak{m}_C C'$, is nilpotent.
--
--   A routine base-change package, of the kind used when passing from an Artin local coefficient ring $C$ with finite residue field to its tensor product with a $\mathbb{Z}$-flat Noetherian ring such as a complete discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field. It is used in the construction of a faithfully flat local extension of $C$ with algebraically closed residue field, [`IsArtinianRing.exists_faithfullyFlat_isLocalHom_isAlgClosed_residueField_of_finite_residueField`](thm.html#IsArtinianRing.exists_faithfullyFlat_isLocalHom_isAlgClosed_residueField_of_finite_residueField).
